POSITIONING = [
 ("What exactly is the product?", "A multi-tenant enterprise LMS. Each customer gets a fully isolated, white-labelled database. It combines course delivery (on-demand, SCORM/xAPI, quizzes, live ILT/VILT), a living skill matrix scored against role targets, rule-based compliance campaigns with auto-certification, eight enterprise reports with branded Excel/PDF exports, cost & ROI analytics, and built-in enterprise identity (OIDC/SAML SSO, SCIM 2.0, JIT)."),
 ("What business problem does it solve?", "Completions don't prove capability. Compliance is tracked by hand and becomes a fire drill at audit time. Reporting is slow and not board-ready. Learning is spread across video, LMS and live-session tools. IT must handle SSO, provisioning and data isolation for every vendor. Leadership can't see training ROI."),
 ("Who needs it?", "Economic buyers: CHRO / Head of L&D, Compliance heads; IT as an influencer (SSO/SCIM, isolation). Users: platform/tenant admins, department-scoped delegated admins, managers, learners."),
 ("What industries can use it?", "Cross-industry; the official site lists IT & Software, BFSI, Healthcare, Manufacturing, Retail, Professional Services. Regulated sectors (BFSI, healthcare) are the strongest fit for compliance automation."),
 ("Primary value proposition", "Measure capability, not completions. Every employee is scored against the skill levels their role needs, compliance runs itself, and leadership gets defensible reporting and ROI — in an isolated, white-labelled tenant with identity built in."),
 ("Core capabilities", "Catalog & courses; on-demand & live learning; skill matrix & development plans; compliance campaigns & certificates; 8 enterprise reports; cost & ROI; people & onboarding; delegated admin; identity (SSO/SCIM/JIT); SCORM/xAPI; LTI 1.3 registry; platform console with metering."),
 ("What makes it different?", "(1) Living skill matrix: completing a course raises the learner's real skill level against role targets. (2) Self-running compliance: rule-based assignment, reminders, certificates with expiry. (3) Identity included, not a paid add-on (per deck). (4) A dedicated database per tenant. (5) Branded, board-ready Excel and PDF."),
 ("Why should a customer evaluate it?", "It answers the question other LMSs can't: 'can our people do the job, and can we prove it at audit time?' A 30-day all-features trial (per decks) lowers evaluation cost."),
 ("Business value", "Audit-ready compliance evidence; visible skill gaps and targeted development; cost per completion and hours delivered for budget decisions; less IT effort through SSO/SCIM. Only demo-data figures exist (73.6% capability match, 86% compliant, Rs 1,800 per completion). They must be labelled as demo data."),
]
